    Imagine that you are part of the team trying to make an AI more robust. Think about the
    following questions.

    ⁉️ Is the source of the data used by the AI model important to know?
    🔊 The source of the data is very important to know. AI models depend on data to learn, so data
    quality is crucial to trustworthy AI. In particular, it is important to know how the data was
    collected, who has access to it, and how it has been used.

    ⁉️ Is it better to use public data? Should the data be screened before it is used?
    🔊 It is neither better nor worse to use public data. Public data can be helpful, but it needs 
    to be carefully vetted before use.

    ⁉️ How would you monitor for attacks on the deployed model?
    🔊 Using a tool to proactively monitor for attacks on a deployed model, like IBM AI Robustness
    360, would be a good strategy.